phi-transport-cli (0.0~git202609101418.994e162-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * `phi-cli backend intents` prints cmd.host.intents.list: what each
    rule under /usr/share/phi/intents asked for and what became of
    it. A rule that means nothing right now prints under the name
    kind@*, because an empty table would read as "no package asked
    for anything".

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:18:01 +0200

phi-transport-cli (0.0~git202609101408.7f1ad7c-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * phi-cli speaks the host layer: radio list/probe/claim/release and
    backend list/create/remove/start/stop/restart, driving
    cmd.host.radio.* and cmd.host.backend* from a terminal instead of
    only the settings page's WebSocket-by-hand path.
  * Fixes a refusal that read as a success: a command core declines
    comes back as accepted:false rather than a rejected ack, and
    sendCommand only read the ack, so every cmd.* this client sends
    could misreport why it failed.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:08:12 +0200

phi-transport-cli (0.0~git202609090827.1cb100d-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * phi-cli is Qt-free, which takes the last Qt6 binary out of this repo: the
    socket is poll() on a non-blocking descriptor, JSON is nlohmann, and the
    envelope types, response topics and cid rules come from the transport api
    instead of being typed out a second time.
  * Output and exit codes are unchanged against the Qt build, command by
    command. Two differences on purpose: nlohmann writes an empty object as
    {} on one line, and `transport reload cli` - which drops the socket it
    was asked through - now says the connection closed instead of reporting a
    timeout that never happened.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 08:27:27 +0200

